# Converge ERP — one ignore file for the whole repo (server + frontend).
#
# Reminder: .gitignore only affects files git is not ALREADY tracking. If
# something ignored here still shows up in `git status`, it is tracked and needs
# `git rm --cached <path>` once to drop it from the index (the file stays on
# disk). That is how node_modules and bin/obj came to be committed here.

# ── Secrets — never commit ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Real credentials live in converge_server/.env (Groq, Resend, M360 SMS, Google
# OAuth) and the Google service-account key is a gen-lang-client-*.json.
# appsettings.json is ignored too because connection strings are kept in it;
# appsettings.Development.json holds only log levels and stays tracked.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
converge_server/appsettings.json
converge_frontend/appsettings.json
**/gen-lang-client-*.json
*.pfx
*.p12
*.pem
*.key

# ── .NET build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# bin/ matters for more than size: the build copies .env and the service-account
# key next to the DLLs, so a tracked bin/ leaks them a second time.
**/bin/
**/obj/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/
*.userprefs

# ── Node / Vite ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ── Editors / OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Local tooling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-developer Claude Code settings. A shared .claude/settings.json, if one is
# ever added, is deliberately still tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json

# ── Runtime uploads ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Proof-of-transaction images and product photos are uploaded by users at run
# time and deleted by the app (removing an attachment deletes the file), so a
# tracked copy is a file the repository keeps resurrecting after the app has
# thrown it away. The directories are kept via .gitkeep so a fresh clone still
# has somewhere to write. A missing evidence file degrades gracefully — the
# item shows "attachment file is missing, click to upload a replacement".
converge_server/wwwroot/images/evidence/*
converge_server/wwwroot/images/products/*
!converge_server/wwwroot/images/evidence/.gitkeep
!converge_server/wwwroot/images/products/.gitkeep

# ── Logs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
